Since  $\angle OBF = \angle OFD = 90^\circ$ , lines  $FB$  and  $FD$  are tangent to  $\omega$ . Therefore,  $\overline{BD}$  is the polar of  $F$  with respect to  $\omega$ . Next, define  $X = \overline{AE}\cap\overline{BD}$ . By La Hire's Theorem,  $F$  must lie on the polar of  $X$ . Furthermore, by Brocard's Theorem on cyclic quadrilateral  $ABDE$ , we have that  $C$  also lies on the polar of  $X$ . Hence,  $\overline{CF}$  is the polar of  $X$  with respect to  $\omega$ . This implies that  $O$ ,  $G$ ,  $X$  are collinear since  $\overline{CF}$  and  $\overline{OX}$  are perpendicular at  $G$ . Finally, by Power of a Point,
\[ XE\cdot XA = XD\cdot XB = XG\cdot XO, \]
so  $O$ ,  $G$ ,  $E$ ,  $A$  are concyclic by the Inverse of Power of a Point.  $\blacksquare$

