Rewrite the statement by considering everything from triangle  $ACE$ .**New Statement:** In an acute triangle  $ABC$  with  $AB\neq AC$ , points  $P$  and  $Q$  are chosen such that  $AP=CP, AQ=BQ$  and  $\measuredangle BAP=\measuredangle CAQ=90$ . Let  $X$  be the intersection of perpendicular bisectors of  $PQ$  and  $BC$ . Prove that  $180-\measuredangle PXQ=2\measuredangle BAC$ .
*Solution.* Let  $O$  be the center of  $(ABC)$ . Let  $Y$  be the center of  $(BOC)$ . We claim that  $X\equiv Y$ .
[asy]
unitsize(4cm);
import geometry;
 pair A,B,C,O,Y,P,Q;
 A=dir(135); B=dir(210); C=dir(330); O=circumcenter(A,B,C); Y=circumcenter(B,O,C);  P=intersectionpoint(perpendicular(A,line(A,B)),perpendicular((A+C)/2,line(A,C)));  Q=intersectionpoint(perpendicular(A,line(A,C)),perpendicular((A+B)/2,line(A,B))); filldraw(O--Y--C--P--cycle,paleblue); filldraw(O--Y--B--Q--cycle,palered);filldraw(A--P--O--Q--cycle,lightgreen); 
 draw(A--B--C--cycle,blue); draw(A--P--C,purple); draw(A--Q--B,purple); draw(P--O--Q,purple);
label(“ $A$ ”,A,dir(A)); label(“ $B$ ”,B,dir(B)); label(“ $C$ ”,C,dir(C)); label(“ $O$ ”,O,dir(O)); label(“ $P$ ”,P,dir(P)); label(“ $Q$ ”,Q,dir(Q)); label(“ $Y$ ”,Y,dir(Y));
dot(A);dot(B);dot(C);dot(O);dot(P);dot(Q);dot(Y);
[/asy]
Note that  $AP\perp AB\perp QO$  and  $AQ\perp AC\perp PO$  so  $APOQ$  is parallelogram.  $PC=PA=QO,QB=QA=PO,BY=OY=CY,OB=OC$  give that  $YOQB$  and  $YCPO$  are congruent. Thus  $YP=YQ$  and  $Y\equiv X$ . So  $\measuredangle PXQ=\measuredangle PYQ=\measuredangle OYB=2\measuredangle OCB=180-2\measuredangle BAC$  and done.

