|f(x)|& =| f(\lfloor x \rfloor + \{x\})|\ge| f(1013+\{x\})|=\{x\}\prod_{i=1}^{1012}\left(i^2-\{x\}^2\right)
&=\{x\}(1012!)^2\prod_{i=1}^{1012}\left(1-\frac{\{x\}^2}{i^2}\right)\ge\{x\}(1012!)^2\left(1-\sum_{i=1}^{1012}\frac{\{x\}^2}{i^2}\right)
&\ge\{x\}(1012!)^2\left(1-\frac{\pi^2}6\cdot\frac14\right)>\frac1{2024!}(1012!)^2\cdot\frac12\textcolor{red}{{}>{}}\frac1{2^{2024}}.
\end{align*}
The last inequality is equivalent to  $\mathrm C_{2024}^{1012}<2^{2023}$ , which follows from the result [here](https://math.stackexchange.com/questions/58560/elementary-central-binomial-coefficient-estimates). Thus, we obtain a contradiction, and the proof is complete.

